WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.380
The east route sounds crisp again.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.760
Then a hearing clinic calls.

3
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:05.580
They play test whistles down the line.

4
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.900
At five thousand hertz,

5
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.140
every patient hears a clear,

6
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.320
steady whistle,
and matches it to three thousand.

7
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:11.720
Not a fuzzy five thousand.

8
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.360
A clean, wrong three thousand.

9
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.030
So a patient who can't hear
five thousand still says yes.

10
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.790
The whistle really is five thousand.

11
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.690
And your boost is linear
and time-invariant,

12
00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.810
so it can't turn one tone into another.

13
00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.350
It happens at the step
where sound becomes numbers.

14
00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:29.050
The sound going into the phone
is the true tone, a smooth wobble.

15
00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.890
But a phone only works with numbers.

16
00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.370
Eight thousand times a second,
it takes one sample.

17
00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.570
That's the sampling rate.

18
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.890
In between, it looks away.

19
00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.850
The list of samples
is what the phone stores,

20
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.370
and nothing else survives.

21
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.370
Sample the whistle, five thousand hertz.

22
00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.930
One, minus point seven one,
zero, point seven one.

23
00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:46.710
Now a real three thousand hertz tone.

24
00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.970
One, minus point seven one,
zero, point seven one.

25
00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.650
The same list, sample for sample.

26
00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.310
Two different waves, the same dots.

27
00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:53.850
Why?

28
00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.030
Lesson three's wheel.

29
00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.170
Each sample,
the dot turns forty-five degrees

30
00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.430
for every thousand hertz,

31
00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.710
and the sample
is how far left or right it sits.

32
00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:02.890
Three thousand turns
one hundred thirty-five degrees,

33
00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:03.910
to the upper left.

34
00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.650
The whistle turns two hundred twenty-five,

35
00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.590
past half a turn, to the lower left.

36
00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.350
Mirror spots, the same reading.

37
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.980
Two hundred twenty-five

38
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.560
is one hundred thirty-five short

39
00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:13.560
of a full turn.

40
00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.660
So the whistle looks like
a three thousand hertz dot

41
00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.740
turning backwards, and samples
can't tell backwards from forwards.

42
00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:19.860
It's the cinema wheel.

43
00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:22.000
A fast car wheel, filmed too rarely,

44
00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.460
seems to creep backwards.

45
00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:25.830
Sweep the true tone up.

46
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:29.310
The stored tone climbs with it
to four thousand hertz, then turns round.

47
00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.390
That's the limit, half the sampling rate.

48
00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:34.330
Above it, the phone stores a lower,
false tone with the same samples,

49
00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:35.250
an alias.

50
00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:36.410
Fold the strip at the limit.

51
00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.850
Five thousand sits one thousand above.

52
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.370
So it lands one thousand below,
on three thousand.

53
00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:43.890
It doesn't blur the tone.

54
00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.890
It moves it, to a perfectly clean one.

55
00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.370
And no program can move it back,

56
00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:49.550
because the whistle's list is,
number for number,

57
00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:51.610
the list of a real
three thousand hertz tone.

58
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.000
The fix has to come before sampling,
while five thousand

59
00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.540
is still five thousand.

60
00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.180
Put a filter in front of the sampler,

61
00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.920
a small circuit that keeps the voice,

62
00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.620
up to three thousand four hundred hertz,

63
00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.420
and fades out the tones above it.

64
00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:06.380
The tone where it switches
from keeping to removing is its cutoff,

65
00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.580
here four thousand.

66
00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.480
The whistle never reaches the sampler,

67
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.500
and the clinic gets honest silence.

68
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:13.820
The line is clean.

69
00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.180
Then it joins a wideband line
at sixteen thousand samples a second.

70
00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.520
Every voice that crosses over
brings a faint ghost copy of itself

71
00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.880
above four thousand hertz,
where nobody was speaking.

72
00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.720
Where do those ghosts come from?
